## How to Compile
make mscopier.cpp
make mmcopier.cpp

## How to Run

## Task 1:
./mmcopier n source_dir destination_dir
Example: ./mmcopier 3 source_dir destination_dir

## Task 2:
1) make clean
2) make mscopier
3) ./generate_text.sh n > source.txt
4) ./mscopier n source.txt destination.txt

Example:
* If you want to generate a new text file from a source file with 500 random lines and 4 writer/reader threads:
make clean
make mscopier
./generate_text.sh 500 > source.txt (Takes 500 unique lines from dictionary file and print to stdout)
./mscopier 4 source.txt destination.txt (spins up 4 reader and writer threads, cordinates them via shared queue, mutexes and condition variables you implemeneted)

## Notes
- destination_dir must already exist before running.
- source_dir exist and contains source1.txt through to source10.txt
- Must run generate_text.sh before i can run rest of mscopier commands (See task 2 example for more context)
- Makefile is setup, make (mmcopier.cpp / mscopier.cpp) compiles addressed file and make clean, will clean both compilations
